  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Keep the UK in the EU; defend the Human Rights Act and ECHR; oppose mass surveillance in favor of targeted, overseen powers. Shape immigration to Scotland’s needs including restoring post‑study work visas; appoint an LGBTI rights envoy; extend votes to 16–17; mandate equal pay audits and promote a living wage. Lead on carbon reduction and climate justice; expand renewables; maintain a fracking moratorium; oppose new nuclear and block Trident renewal.\n\nTEXT_D: Leave the EU via Article 50; restore UK sovereignty over law and tax; leave the ECHR and enact a UK Bill of Rights. Impose a five‑year moratorium on unskilled immigration; points‑based system; five years’ contributions before full benefits/NHS; no amnesty; revoke citizenship for terrorists; increase Border Force and police/prison staff; deport foreign offenders; zero‑tolerance on antisocial behavior. Promote British values and integration; restrict general election voting to citizens; raise defense to 2%+ of GDP and retain Trident. Repeal the Climate Change Act; end subsidies for onshore wind/solar; back shale, coal, and nuclear.",
  "reasoning": "The electorate profile leans TAN (0.60), prioritizing national identity, order, and sovereignty. TEXT_D explicitly argues from TAN commitments—sovereignty over the EU/ECHR, restrictive immigration, law‑and‑order, traditional/national identity—whereas TEXT_C argues from GAL commitments like supranationalism, expanded civil liberties, social liberalization, and environmentalism.",
